(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["anatomy-exam-3-female-reproductive-quiz-version-6"]={"title":"Female Reproductive System — Anatomy Exam 3 (Set 6)","category":"Anatomy","sem":"summer-1-2026","questions":[{"q":"The perineum is bounded anteriorly by the pubic symphysis, laterally by the ischial tuberosities, and posteriorly by which structure?","choices":["The ischial spines","The pubic arch","The sacrum","The coccyx"],"answer":3,"exp":"The perineum is circumscribed posteriorly by the coccyx. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 5"},{"q":"The two triangular subdivisions of the perineum are separated by an imaginary horizontal line extending between which structures?","choices":["The ischial spines","The anterior superior iliac spines","The ischial tuberosities","The pubic tubercles"],"answer":2,"exp":"An imaginary horizontal line between the ischial tuberosities separates the perineum into the anterior (urogenital) and posterior (anal) triangles. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 5"},{"q":"In females, the anterior (urogenital) triangle of the perineum contains which structures?","choices":["The base of the penis and scrotum","The anus only","The coccyx","The urethral and vaginal orifices"],"answer":3,"exp":"In females, the urogenital triangle contains the urethral and vaginal orifices. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 5"},{"q":"The boundaries of the female perineum include the mons pubis anteriorly, the medial thighs laterally, and which structures posteriorly?","choices":["The labia majora","The ischial tuberosities","The pubic symphysis","The gluteal folds"],"answer":3,"exp":"The gluteal folds, at the superior end of the intergluteal cleft where the coccyx is palpable, form the posterior boundary of the perineum. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 8"},{"q":"The pelvic diaphragm is formed by the levator ani and which other muscle?","choices":["Obturator internus","Iliopsoas","Piriformis","Coccygeus"],"answer":3,"exp":"The pelvic diaphragm is formed by the levator ani and coccygeus muscles. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 9"},{"q":"The levator ani muscle is made up of the puborectalis, pubococcygeus, and which third component?","choices":["Ischiococcygeus","Pubovaginalis","Bulbospongiosus","Iliococcygeus"],"answer":3,"exp":"The levator ani is composed of the puborectalis, pubococcygeus, and iliococcygeus. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 9"},{"q":"Which of the following is a stated function of the pelvic diaphragm?","choices":["Supporting pelvic organs and sealing the inferior pelvic opening","Producing cervical mucus that varies with the cycle","Producing estrogen and progesterone continuously","Forming the broad ligament that suspends the uterus"],"answer":0,"exp":"The pelvic diaphragm supports the pelvic organs, seals the inferior opening of the bony pelvis, and lifts to help release feces during defecation. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 9"},{"q":"The anterior peritoneal recess between the uterus and urinary bladder is called the:","choices":["Rectouterine pouch","Paravesical fossa","Pararectal fossa","Vesicouterine pouch"],"answer":3,"exp":"The vesicouterine pouch is the anterior recess between the uterus and the urinary bladder. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 12"},{"q":"The posterior peritoneal recess between the uterus and the rectum is called the:","choices":["Ovarian fossa","Rectouterine pouch","Broad ligament","Vesicouterine pouch"],"answer":1,"exp":"The rectouterine pouch is the posterior recess between the uterus anteriorly and the rectum posteriorly. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 12"},{"q":"Which double fold of peritoneum attaches the ovaries to the broad ligament?","choices":["Mesosalpinx","Mesovarium","Round ligament","Mesometrium"],"answer":1,"exp":"The mesovarium is the double fold of peritoneum attaching the ovaries to the broad ligament. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 14"},{"q":"The suspensory ligament of the ovary connects the ovary to which structure?","choices":["The urinary bladder","The uterus","The pelvic wall","The rectum"],"answer":2,"exp":"The suspensory ligament of the ovary extends from the ovary to the pelvic wall. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 14"},{"q":"The Müllerian (paramesonephric) ducts arise from the coelomic epithelium on the lateral aspect of the mesonephros at approximately which week of development?","choices":["12th week","6th week","3rd week","20th week"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Müllerian ducts arise from coelomic epithelium around the 6th week of development. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 16"},{"q":"The Müllerian ducts develop into the female reproductive organs specifically in the absence of which hormone?","choices":["Testosterone from the fetal testes","Anti-Müllerian hormone (AMH)","Estradiol from ovarian tissue","Progesterone from the placenta"],"answer":1,"exp":"In the absence of anti-Müllerian hormone (AMH), the Müllerian ducts persist and develop into the major internal female reproductive organs. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 16"},{"q":"The caudal portions of the Müllerian ducts fuse in the midline to form the:","choices":["Urogenital sinus cavity","Uterovaginal primordium","Gubernaculum ligament","Mesonephric duct remnant"],"answer":1,"exp":"The fused caudal portions of the Müllerian ducts form the uterovaginal primordium. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 16"},{"q":"The upper one-third of the vagina develops from the fused Müllerian ducts, while the lower vagina develops from the:","choices":["Mesonephric duct","Yolk sac","Allantois","Urogenital sinus"],"answer":3,"exp":"The lower vagina develops from the urogenital sinus, while the upper vagina develops from the fused Müllerian ducts. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 16"},{"q":"Venous drainage of the right ovary empties into which vessel?","choices":["The inferior vena cava","The external iliac vein","The left renal vein","The internal iliac vein"],"answer":0,"exp":"The right ovary drains venously into the inferior vena cava, while the left ovary drains into the left renal vein. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 24"},{"q":"Venous drainage of the left ovary empties into which vessel?","choices":["The left renal vein","The internal iliac vein","The splenic vein","The inferior vena cava directly"],"answer":0,"exp":"The left ovary drains into the left renal vein, while the right ovary drains directly into the inferior vena cava. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 24"},{"q":"Venous drainage of the ovaries occurs via which named venous network?","choices":["Pampiniform plexus","Uterine venous plexus","Vesical venous plexus","Presacral venous plexus"],"answer":0,"exp":"Ovarian veins drain via the pampiniform plexus before continuing to the IVC (right) or left renal vein (left). — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"Lymphatics of the ovaries follow the ovarian blood vessels to ascend to which lymph nodes?","choices":["Axillary lymph nodes","Lumbar (para-aortic) lymph nodes","Superficial inguinal lymph nodes","Deep cervical lymph nodes"],"answer":1,"exp":"Ovarian lymphatics follow the ovarian blood vessels to ascend to the lumbar lymph nodes. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"Parasympathetic innervation of the ovary arises from which nerves?","choices":["Pudendal nerve","Pelvic splanchnic nerves","Vagus nerve fibers","Greater splanchnic nerve"],"answer":1,"exp":"Parasympathetic innervation of the ovary arises from the pelvic splanchnic nerves. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"The cardinal and uterosacral ligaments supporting the uterus are described as thickenings of which tissue?","choices":["Dense cartilage tissue","Skeletal muscle tissue only","Peritoneum without muscular component","Subserous fascia and smooth muscle"],"answer":3,"exp":"The cardinal and uterosacral ligaments are thickenings of subserous fascia and smooth muscle. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 31"},{"q":"The uterus is described as being anteverted at the junction of which two structures?","choices":["Cervix and vagina","Cervix and body","Body and fundus","Isthmus and body"],"answer":0,"exp":"The uterus is anteverted at the junction of the cervix and vagina. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 31"},{"q":"The uterus is described as being anteflexed at the junction of which two structures?","choices":["Cervix and body","Isthmus and cervix","Fundus and uterine tube","Cervix and vagina"],"answer":0,"exp":"The uterus is anteflexed at the junction of the cervix and body. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 31"},{"q":"The isthmus of the uterus is the constricted region located between which two parts?","choices":["Fundus and cervix","Cervix and vagina","Fundus and body","Body and cervix"],"answer":3,"exp":"The isthmus is the constricted region between the body and cervix of the uterus. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 34"},{"q":"The fundus of the uterus is described as the rounded portion located:","choices":["Superior and anterior to the uterine tube entrance","Inferior to the cervix near the vaginal fornix","Located entirely within the vaginal canal","Directly posterior to the rectum and sacrum"],"answer":0,"exp":"The fundus is the rounded portion of the uterus superior and anterior to the entrance of the uterine tubes. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 34"},{"q":"The opening of the cervix into the vagina is called the:","choices":["Fornix","External os","Isthmus","Internal os"],"answer":1,"exp":"The external os is the opening of the cervix into the vagina. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 34"},{"q":"The opening of the cervix into the uterine isthmus is called the:","choices":["External os","Cervical canal","Fornix","Internal os"],"answer":3,"exp":"The internal os is the opening of the cervix into the uterine isthmus. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 34"},{"q":"In the nonpregnant uterus, myometrial smooth muscle cells are typically less than what length?","choices":["25 mm","0.025 mm","0.25 mm","2.5 mm"],"answer":2,"exp":"In the nonpregnant uterus, myometrial smooth muscle cells are less than 0.25 millimeters in length. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 39"},{"q":"The perimetrium, the outer tunic of most of the uterus, is continuous with which structure?","choices":["The broad ligament","The rectum","The vagina","The round ligament"],"answer":0,"exp":"The perimetrium, a serosa, is continuous with the broad ligament. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 39"},{"q":"The two layers of the endometrium are the stratum functionalis and the:","choices":["Stratum corneum","Stratum spinosum","Stratum germinativum","Stratum basalis"],"answer":3,"exp":"The two layers of the endometrium are the stratum functionalis and the stratum basalis. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 43"}]};
